{
  "target": "src.services.order_service:OrderService",
  "diagnosis": "The OrderService class exhibits a critical lack of cohesion (LCOM4=5) and high complexity (WMC=56, NOM=26), indicating it is a 'God Class' that conflates four distinct responsibilities: order lifecycle management, pricing logic, audit logging, and notification handling. The high LCOM4 score confirms that methods are partitioned into disconnected clusters, each operating on a separate set of attributes (e.g., _repository vs. _tax_rate vs. _audit). This design violates the Single Responsibility Principle, making the class difficult to test, maintain, and reuse, as changes to pricing rules, for instance, require modifying a class that also manages order persistence and notifications.",
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "title": "Extract Pricing Logic into a PricingService",
      "rationale_metric_link": [
        "LCOM4",
        "WMC",
        "NOM"
      ],
      "expected_effect": [
        {
          "metric": "LCOM4",
          "direction": "down",
          "confidence": 0.9
        },
        {
          "metric": "WMC",
          "direction": "down",
          "confidence": 0.8
        },
        {
          "metric": "NOM",
          "direction": "down",
          "confidence": 0.9
        }
      ],
      "sketch": "Move methods set_discount, discount_for, bulk_discount, set_tax_rate, apply_tax, total_for, policy_rate, and is_priced, along with attributes _tax_rate and _discounts, into a new PricingService class. OrderService should delegate pricing calculations to this new service. This reduces the number of methods and complexity in OrderService and isolates pricing rules, which are likely to change independently of order lifecycle logic."
    },
    {
      "title": "Extract Audit Logging into an AuditLogger",
      "rationale_metric_link": [
        "LCOM4",
        "NOM"
      ],
      "expected_effect": [
        {
          "metric": "LCOM4",
          "direction": "down",
          "confidence": 0.9
        },
        {
          "metric": "NOM",
          "direction": "down",
          "confidence": 0.8
        }
      ],
      "sketch": "Move methods log, history, last_entry, audit_size, and clear_audit, along with the _audit attribute, into a dedicated AuditLogger class. OrderService should hold a reference to this logger and delegate audit calls. This removes a distinct cluster of methods from OrderService, further improving cohesion."
    },
    {
      "title": "Extract Notification Handling into a NotificationService",
      "rationale_metric_link": [
        "LCOM4",
        "NOM"
      ],
      "expected_effect": [
        {
          "metric": "LCOM4",
          "direction": "down",
